{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>His ornaments</b> — three times in the Masorah: דין ואידך וצבי עדיו לגאון שמהו. במתג ורסן עדיו לבלום. Because they grew proud with the ornaments of a gazelle's glory, as the Sages interpreted — on account of the abundance of silver and gold that was given them, they made the golden calf — therefore 'no man put on his ornaments,' and their mouths were stopped, for they had no opening of the mouth, like a bit and bridle that curb a horse's ornaments."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:00.573199390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}